+---
+name: mira-primary-courseware
+title: "Mira 小学精品课"
+description: "Mira 小学一二年级精品课件设计。用于生成或重做低年级语文、数学、英语课堂，强调具体操作、单页单目标、逐步聚焦、可观察练习和短句旁白；联网只用于确有时效性的外部事实，不用于基础课本知识。"
+---
+
+# Mira primary courseware
+
+Build one calm, concrete and genuinely teachable early-primary classroom. Load
+stage-design first. Also load k12-core-literacy-planning when the request names
+curriculum standards, core literacy or a subject performance task. For an
+existing stage, follow pro-editing and repair only the weak pages.
+
+## Learning arc
+
+Set one bounded skill and one visible success condition. Prefer 6–8 pages:
+
+1. a familiar situation and one question;
+2. concrete objects, sound, movement or visual grouping;
+3. the rule or pattern discovered from that evidence;
+4. one worked example with the reason shown step by step;
+5. guided manipulation or choice with immediate explanatory feedback;
+6. one diagnostic check aimed at the most likely misconception;
+7. transfer to a small new situation;
+8. optional recap that names the method in the learner's own words.
+
+The learner must do something on at least every second page. Do not produce a
+sequence of static definition slides.
+
+## Page craft
+
+- One page, one teaching move. Use a short action title, not “知识讲解”,
+  “案例分析” or “课堂总结”.
+- Design for a six-to-eight-year-old viewing from a distance: large type, short
+  phrases, strong figure-ground contrast and no dense card grids.
+- Prefer concrete objects, number lines, sound blocks, letter tiles, position
+  maps and before/after states over decorative illustration.
+- Every visual must teach, scaffold or receive an action. Decoration never
+  substitutes for an explanation.
+- A worked example reveals one step at a time and explains why. A quiz uses
+  plausible misconceptions and feedback that teaches the correction.
+- Interactive pages must change a meaningful state and make the consequence
+  visible. Never label a static picture as a game, simulation or 3D.
+
+## Narration and focus
+
+Write short conversational narration with one instruction per sentence. On
+each explanatory slide, bind the relevant speech line to an existing element
+with set_spotlight; the spotlight target must be the exact object, word, step
+or answer being discussed. Do not dim a page without a valid target.
+
+Read every generated page back. If the layout is dense, the target is missing
+or narration talks about something not visible, repair it before moving on.
+Generate TTS after the final narration and spotlight sequence is settled.
+
+## Controlled research
+
+Foundational primary-school knowledge does not need web research. Use
+web_search only when the lesson depends on current, named or externally
+checkable facts. In that case:
+
+- make at most four precise searches for the whole course;
+- prefer primary and authoritative sources;
+- fetch and read the source before using a claim;
+- include source name and date in the page brief;
+- never invent a citation or turn an unverified result into learner-facing
+  fact.
+
+Student playback never receives search tools. Formal Mira catalog generation
+also keeps web search off; this research branch is for an operator deliberately
+building a sourced course in the professional workbench.
+
+## Completion gate
+
+Do not call the classroom complete until every approved page is persisted,
+every speech action has audio, each explanation page has a valid spotlight
+target, at least one misconception is diagnosed, and the final task checks the
+same skill in a new context.
